WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
<b>Calpis theater</b>

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Subs: English

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:14.000
S

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:14.000
<b><i>SILVER ZERO
 SUBS</i></b>

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:14.000
http://silverzerosubs.blogspot.com/

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:33.830
Original story by Johanna Spyri

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:33.830
<b>Alps no Shoujo Heidi</b>

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.090
<u>Why do I hear</u>

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.090
Kuchibue ha naze

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:38.250
<u>the whistling from far away?</u>

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:38.250
Tooku made kikoeru no

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.460
<u>Why is that cloud</u>

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.460
Ano kumo ha naze

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.600
<u>waiting for me?</u>

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.600
Watashi wo matteru no

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.800
<u>Tell me, Grandfather.</u>

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.800
Oshiete ojiisan

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.690
<u>Tell me, Grandfather.</u>

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.690
Oshiete ojiisan

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:59.380
<u>Oh tell me, the fir trees of the Alm.</u>

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:59.380
Oshiete arumu no momi no ki yo

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:27.600
The Mountain Pasture

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:34.530
<i>Morning has come to Alm mountain.</i>

00:01:34.870 --> 00:01:37.580
<i>Heidi, having separated from Aunt Dete,</i>

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:42.210
<i>greets the first morning in
her Grandfather's mountain cabin.</i>

00:01:59.270 --> 00:02:01.230
You're ridiculously early today.

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:03.230
I told you I wouldn't oversleep.

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:08.900
That's right! I'm living in
my grandfather's house.

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:11.700
{++++MJN I'm so happy!}What nice weather!

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:28.790
Grandfather, good morning.

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:30.650
Good morning.

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:34.490
Good morning, Little Swan
and Little Bear.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:36.550
Good morning, Peter.

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:37.950
Good morning.

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:44.820
Good morning, Snowflake.

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:48.340
From the looks of it,
you seem to have slept well.

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:52.140
{++++MJN Well? Do you want to go with them
on to the mountain?}Do you want to go along up there
with the goats? How about it?

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:54.140
Really? Can I go?

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:58.060
{++++MJN But you must first wash
and make yourself tidy.}But wash your face first,

00:02:58.060 --> 00:03:00.120
or the sun will laugh at you.

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:01.880
Peter, wait a little.

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:04.300
Hey, Goat General!

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:06.340
Come here.

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:17.900
Take care she does not fall over
any of the rocks, do you hear?

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:24.090
I've washed myself.

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:27.350
Will the sun laugh at me now?

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:30.210
No, you're all right now.

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:34.370
{++++MJN Will he come with us?}Won't Joseph go with us?

00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:37.220
I don't know.
Will you go, Joseph?

00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:41.080
He just sleeps.

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:45.310
Now, be off with you. And be careful.

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:47.350
I'm going!

00:03:57.460 --> 00:03:59.730
Why can a whistle

00:03:57.460 --> 00:03:59.730
Kuchibue ha naze

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:01.860
be heard from afar?

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:01.860
Tooku made kikoeru no

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:04.150
Why is that cloud

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:04.150
Ano kumo ha naze

00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:06.410
waiting for me?

00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:06.410
Watashi wo matteru no

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:10.640
Tell me, grandfather

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:10.640
Oshiete ojiisan

00:04:10.910 --> 00:04:14.410
Tell me, grandfather

00:04:10.910 --> 00:04:14.410
Oshiete ojiisan

00:04:14.630 --> 00:04:23.090
Oh tell me, the fir trees of the Alm

00:04:14.630 --> 00:04:23.090
Oshiete arumu no momi no ki yo

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:34.310
Why is the mountain snow

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:34.310
Yuki no yama naze

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:36.590
dyed in rose-color?

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:36.590
Barairo ni somaru no

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:39.090
Where is that wind

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:39.090
Ano kaze ha doko ni

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:40.960
hiding?

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:40.960
Kakureteiru no

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:45.030
Tell me, grandfather

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:45.030
Oshiete ojiisan

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:44.700
Beautiful!

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:49.100
Tell me, grandfather

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:49.100
Oshiete ojiisan

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:48.430
Hey!

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:49.660
Wait!

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:57.370
Oh tell me, the fir trees of the Alm

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:57.370
Oshiete arumu no momi no ki yo

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:51.370
Wait!

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:20.320
One, two...

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:26.920
Heidi!

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:32.840
Hey, Heidi!

00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:36.280
I'm here!

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:40.640
Where?

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:47.310
Where are you?

00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:50.760
{***++++MJN Where have you gone to now?}Come out!

00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:52.780
Here!

00:05:54.990 --> 00:05:59.360
{++++MJN Come along here! Your grandfather gave
me orders to not let you fall over the rocks.}Don't run off on your own!
The old man said you mustn't fall off rocks.

00:05:59.360 --> 00:06:01.040
Where are the rocks?

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:05.620
Right up above.
We have a long way to go yet.

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:10.130
{++++MJN And on the topmost peak of all the
old bird of prey sits and croaks.}On top of the rocks, there
lives a really ancient hawk!

00:06:10.130 --> 00:06:11.960
So come along!

00:06:14.790 --> 00:06:16.580
Stop doing that.

00:06:16.590 --> 00:06:19.440
Heidi, you're slower than the goats.

00:06:19.990 --> 00:06:22.560
I want to pick many
flowers to put on my bed.

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:25.770
That way it will seem like I'm sleeping
in a beautiful field of flowers.

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:30.090
But, If you pick so many today,
there won't be any tomorrow.

00:06:32.410 --> 00:06:35.120
{++++MJN The old bird really lives up there.}Hey, there really are hawks on top of the rock!

00:06:36.670 --> 00:06:39.170
{++++And also lives}And the lord with big horns, too.

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:42.960
And the cute things.
Don't you want to see them?

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:48.550
The cute things and the lord of the heights?
They really live up there?

00:06:48.730 --> 00:06:50.840
Really. Let's go.

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:52.310
I'm going.

00:06:58.060 --> 00:06:59.950
What is a cute thing?

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:02.640
It's a cute thing!

00:07:06.630 --> 00:07:08.210
Is that a cute thing?

00:07:08.210 --> 00:07:10.400
Don't be silly.
That's a squirrel.

00:07:10.840 --> 00:07:13.400
That's right.
It also looked like a squirrel to me.

00:07:15.010 --> 00:07:16.530
A rabbit!

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:21.680
Leave it alone.

00:07:21.690 --> 00:07:23.870
But rabbits are cute too, aren't they?

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:26.250
What I'm talking about is cuter than rabbits.

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:27.270
{++++MJN Really?}It's that cute?

00:07:27.270 --> 00:07:29.310
{++++MJN Really. Well, let's go.}I'm telling you! Now, let's go!

00:07:34.060 --> 00:07:36.030
{++++MJN Peter, there it is.}Peter, a hawk!

00:07:38.620 --> 00:07:41.860
{++++MJN That's just a milvus.
You really don't know anything.}That's a mountain crow.
You don't know anything, do you?

00:07:45.210 --> 00:07:46.110
We're almost there.

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:47.000
Let's go.

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:08.790
It's so beautiful.

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:33.750
That's all snow?

00:08:33.750 --> 00:08:34.950
Yes, it is.

00:08:35.090 --> 00:08:37.320
{++++MJN It's so many!}There's so much!

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:44.010
I want to eat it.

00:08:58.620 --> 00:09:02.220
Peter, what's wrong?
Does Your stomach hurts?

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:05.240
No. I'm just going to sleep a little.

00:09:06.210 --> 00:09:08.640
Hey, where are the cute things?

00:09:09.720 --> 00:09:10.880
Hey, Peter.

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:14.800
They're hiding in the rocks.

00:09:15.250 --> 00:09:16.360
Where?

00:09:16.380 --> 00:09:18.340
{++++MJN Shut up. They'll show up later.
Sleep a little.}You make such a fuss!

00:09:18.590 --> 00:09:20.140
If you just wait, they'll show themselves.

00:09:20.180 --> 00:09:21.510
You should rest, too.

00:09:22.830 --> 00:09:27.120
{++++MJN Liar! There are no cute things,
and no lord with big horns here.}You liar! There's no hawk, and
no lord with big horns either!

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:29.570
I'm not lying! There are.

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:34.250
Then, let's go see them!
Come on, let's go see them!

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:39.650
That Peter!

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:45.020
<i>Peter is exhausted and falls fast asleep.</i>

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:46.690
<i>Since he gets up early in the morning...</i>

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:50.440
<i>and gathers the goats from throughout
the village, this is not surprising.</i>

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:54.910
<i>But Heidi, who is here for the first
time, doesn't feel like that at all.</i>

00:09:55.120 --> 00:09:58.690
<i>The hawk, the cute things
and the lord of the heights...</i>

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:02.120
<i>that Peter had mentioned are on her mind.</i>

00:10:17.980 --> 00:10:19.730
A hawk! There's a hawk!

00:10:29.320 --> 00:10:31.670
Peter! Peter!

00:10:34.220 --> 00:10:35.590
Peter!

00:10:37.450 --> 00:10:39.430
H-Heidi, where are you?

00:10:39.960 --> 00:10:41.400
<i>Peter!</i>

00:10:41.540 --> 00:10:42.910
{++++MJN What happened, Heidi?}What's the matter, Heidi?!

00:10:43.210 --> 00:10:44.680
Peter!

00:10:46.220 --> 00:10:47.160
Heidi!

00:10:48.350 --> 00:10:50.800
Thank goodness.
Help me!

00:10:50.800 --> 00:10:53.370
{++++MJN Don't move or you'll fall.}Don't move! Don't look down!

00:10:54.680 --> 00:10:55.710
There.

00:10:58.330 --> 00:11:01.170
{++++MJN That scared me.
But what were you doing there?}What a relief. But why were you at a place like this?

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:02.850
He tried to eat me.

00:11:05.150 --> 00:11:07.100
{++++MJN Is that the Great Bird?}That's the hawk on the summit, isn't it?

00:11:10.340 --> 00:11:13.150
{++++MJN Yes, but he never attacks people.}Hawks rarely attack people, you know.

00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:21.340
{++++MJN Why does he make that noise?}I wonder why he cries like that.

00:11:21.580 --> 00:11:25.110
{++++MJN Because he can't help it.
Be careful where you walk!}More importantly, it's dangerous
to just walk off like that!

00:11:25.210 --> 00:11:26.110
But...

00:11:26.900 --> 00:11:29.730
{++++MJN Oh! He is going away.}Oh look, the hawk is flying
over to the other mountain.

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:31.220
Where has it gone to?

00:11:31.760 --> 00:11:34.150
Home, to its nest.

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:36.430
{++++MJN Is his home right up there?}On top of that mountain?

00:11:36.610 --> 00:11:39.770
Nice! He has a nest that high up?

00:11:41.610 --> 00:11:42.660
I want to see it.

00:11:43.150 --> 00:11:46.120
Why don't we go over
there to see his nest?

00:11:46.170 --> 00:11:48.990
Are you crazy? We couldn't do it.

00:11:49.720 --> 00:11:52.740
{++++MJN Why even the goats cannot
climb as high as that!}Not even goats can climb that high.

00:11:53.300 --> 00:11:55.670
{++++MJN Only the lord with big horns can do it.}Although the lord with big horns might be able to.

00:11:56.010 --> 00:11:57.280
Come on, let's eat!

00:11:58.330 --> 00:12:00.860
As if the lord of the heights existed.

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:12.760
{++++MJN Those large pieces of bread
and cheese are yours.}Those big ones are yours.

00:12:12.760 --> 00:12:15.970
{++++MJN When you have drunk up that milk, you are
to have another bowlful from the goat.}When you finish your milk,
I'll milk you another cup full.

00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:18.110
{++++MJN Peter, can you milk a goat?}What about your milk?

00:12:30.760 --> 00:12:32.410
I want to do that, too!

00:12:33.810 --> 00:12:36.030
No way.
You can't do it!

00:12:36.030 --> 00:12:37.130
I can!

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:47.630
<i>When it's time to eat, Peter gathers
the goats around him.</i>

00:12:47.830 --> 00:12:52.130
<i>That's convenient for watching
over them and drinking milk.</i>

00:13:19.480 --> 00:13:20.600
You can have this.

00:13:21.490 --> 00:13:23.950
<i>Peter is really surprised.</i>

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:25.700
<i>Until now, getting things from people...</i>

00:13:25.710 --> 00:13:29.750
<i>or being given things in this way has
not happened to him even once.</i>

00:13:31.060 --> 00:13:33.290
{++++MJN Can I have them?
Really?}You're giving this to me... really?

00:13:33.360 --> 00:13:35.880
Yes. I have plenty.

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:37.030
Thank you!

00:13:38.720 --> 00:13:40.610
{++++MJN Can I really eat them?}Is it really okay for me to take this?

00:13:52.690 --> 00:13:55.310
Then, that one is...

00:13:55.590 --> 00:13:56.940
Greenfinch.

00:13:57.150 --> 00:13:58.660
Right! Greenfinch.

00:13:58.920 --> 00:14:00.190
I knew that.

00:14:00.420 --> 00:14:02.410
And that one is,

00:14:02.410 --> 00:14:03.430
the great Turk.

00:14:03.430 --> 00:14:05.010
That's right. The great Turk.

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:10.640
{++++MJN}{++++Hey, Abarenbou's horns or those of the lord
with the big horns, which are bigger?}Hey, which one has the biggest horns?
The great Turk or the lord with big horns?

00:14:11.050 --> 00:14:13.750
{++++MJN The horns of The King
of Horns are bigger. Of course, those of the lord of the heights.}Of course, those of the lord with big horns.

00:14:15.350 --> 00:14:16.950
Oh! Greenfinch!

00:14:17.300 --> 00:14:21.150
{++++MJN She is the only one brave
enough to face him.}He's not grownup yet, so he
doesn't know to be afraid.

00:14:21.700 --> 00:14:24.050
And those are,
Little Swan and Little Bear,

00:14:24.060 --> 00:14:26.500
{++++your goat}Peter's goats and Snowflake.

00:14:26.910 --> 00:14:28.680
{++++MJNWhich one is Snowflake's mother?}Where's Snowflake's mother?

00:14:28.770 --> 00:14:32.800
{++++MJN Her mother was sold at Mayenfeld
the day before yesterday.}She was sold to Maienfeld a long time ago.

00:14:32.800 --> 00:14:34.700
I see, so she was sold.

00:14:37.990 --> 00:14:38.900
Snowflake...

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:41.630
I'm here now, so you're no longer alone.

00:14:42.300 --> 00:14:43.240
Look, look!

00:14:44.440 --> 00:14:45.320
What?

00:14:46.340 --> 00:14:48.020
It's the cute things!

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:50.780
Where? Where are they, Peter?

00:14:50.780 --> 00:14:52.260
They've already hidden themselves.

00:14:53.090 --> 00:14:54.590
Oh no!

00:14:55.850 --> 00:14:57.520
Greenfinch! Come back!

00:14:57.770 --> 00:14:59.860
Greenfinch! That's no good!

00:14:59.980 --> 00:15:01.960
{++++MJN Stop!}You!

00:15:02.550 --> 00:15:03.930
Idiot! Don't struggle!

00:15:06.220 --> 00:15:07.790
Stop it! You'll fall!

00:15:07.820 --> 00:15:08.760
Greenfinch!

00:15:08.770 --> 00:15:10.400
{++++MJN What shall we do?}What should I do?

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:11.850
Stop it!

00:15:16.200 --> 00:15:18.770
{++++MJN Look, Atori!
Come here!}Hey, Greenfinch! Hey, over here!

00:15:19.190 --> 00:15:21.250
{++++MJN I have something delicious for you!}I have some tasty grass for you!

00:15:21.280 --> 00:15:22.300
Come here!

00:15:32.970 --> 00:15:34.120
That scared me.

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:36.970
Just you wait!
Come!

00:15:39.170 --> 00:15:40.730
{++++MJN I'm going to punish you!}You damn rascal!

00:15:41.970 --> 00:15:43.470
Stop, Peter!

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:46.310
{++++MJN She deserves it.}He did something bad.
If I don't hit him, he'll make a habit of it!

00:15:46.810 --> 00:15:49.360
{++++MJN You have no right to touch her.}Don't! He's already so scared!

00:15:53.240 --> 00:15:55.360
{++++MJN Please don't hurt her!}Please, don't hit him!

00:15:55.360 --> 00:15:58.290
Greenfinch, you won't do that anymore, right?

00:16:00.730 --> 00:16:01.570
See?

00:16:04.140 --> 00:16:09.230
{++++MJN Well, Heidi. If I let her off will you give me
some more of your cheese tomorrow?}Well, Heidi, if I forgive Greenfinch,
will you give me your cheese again?

00:16:10.250 --> 00:16:13.460
Yes! You shall have it all my
cheese and bread.

00:16:13.460 --> 00:16:17.230
Tomorrow and also after that.
So, don't hit Greenfinch...

00:16:17.230 --> 00:16:20.110
or Snowflake, or any other goat, okay?

00:16:22.900 --> 00:16:24.320
Oh well...

00:16:26.100 --> 00:16:27.000
{++++MJN Then go.}Greenfinch, off you go.

00:16:40.710 --> 00:16:45.620
The treetops

00:16:40.710 --> 00:16:45.620
Kozue ha sotto

00:16:46.810 --> 00:16:51.970
are swaying gently

00:16:46.810 --> 00:16:51.970
Yureteite

00:16:52.920 --> 00:16:58.720
The evening sun is coloring

00:16:52.920 --> 00:16:58.720
Yuuhi ja yama wo

00:16:59.250 --> 00:17:06.260
the mountains

00:16:59.250 --> 00:17:06.260
Someteite

00:17:02.100 --> 00:17:04.390
Come on, let's go home!

00:17:08.620 --> 00:17:11.070
I can hear

00:17:08.620 --> 00:17:11.070
Dare ka ga

00:17:11.730 --> 00:17:14.110
the sound

00:17:11.730 --> 00:17:14.110
Kuchibue

00:17:14.930 --> 00:17:20.260
Narashiteru

00:17:24.100 --> 00:17:26.030
Come here,

00:17:24.100 --> 00:17:26.030
Oide

00:17:26.490 --> 00:17:28.320
little goat,

00:17:26.490 --> 00:17:28.320
Koyagi

00:17:28.750 --> 00:17:34.390
it's time to go home

00:17:28.750 --> 00:17:34.390
Mou kaerou yo

00:17:34.800 --> 00:17:39.240
Down to that green

00:17:34.800 --> 00:17:39.240
Ano midori no

00:17:39.610 --> 00:17:46.500
fir tree

00:17:39.610 --> 00:17:46.500
Momi no shita he

00:17:50.560 --> 00:17:55.010
I didn't get to see the
cute things and the lord of the heights.

00:17:55.530 --> 00:17:56.860
You'll see them next time.

00:18:06.990 --> 00:18:09.740
Peter! Peter! They're on fire!

00:18:09.740 --> 00:18:11.660
The mountains are all on fire!

00:18:11.780 --> 00:18:15.240
Those clouds over there, too,
and the snow, everything's on fire!

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:17.020
It is always like that...

00:18:17.020 --> 00:18:20.670
but it is not really fire.
It gets like that of itself.

00:18:21.710 --> 00:18:24.200
Oh! Look, the lord of the heights!

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:30.280
And there are the cute things!
Look, look!

00:19:08.810 --> 00:19:13.370
Look, look!
Now they have turned all rose color!

00:19:20.250 --> 00:19:25.810
{++++MJN What's wrong? Now they are turning grey!
Now all the colors have died away!}What's wrong? They disappeared!
Everything is gone.

00:19:29.630 --> 00:19:34.990
It will come again tomorrow. Come on,
we must go home now. Let's go.

00:19:39.330 --> 00:19:40.400
Peter!

00:19:41.470 --> 00:19:43.880
Is it like that every day?

00:19:44.020 --> 00:19:45.300
Most of the days.

00:19:45.300 --> 00:19:47.080
But will it be like that tomorrow for certain?

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:49.300
Yes. Tomorrow for certain.

00:19:49.340 --> 00:19:50.530
I'm glad.

00:20:06.460 --> 00:20:08.040
I'm back!

00:20:09.260 --> 00:20:13.240
Welcome back.
So how did you like it?

00:20:13.240 --> 00:20:16.250
I loved it! I'm going back tomorrow.

00:20:16.260 --> 00:20:18.990
{++++MJN Come with me again tomorrow!
Good night!}See you tomorrow! Good night!

00:20:19.580 --> 00:20:21.910
Goodbye, Peter!

00:20:22.420 --> 00:20:24.800
Goodnight, Snowflake!

00:20:30.150 --> 00:20:32.540
Grandfather, it was so beautiful.

00:20:33.220 --> 00:20:37.050
The fire, the roses on the rocks, the lord
of the heights and the cute things!

00:20:37.050 --> 00:20:39.460
And look what I have brought you!

00:20:46.250 --> 00:20:48.390
What is the matter with them?

00:20:49.050 --> 00:20:49.970
What...

00:20:50.240 --> 00:20:51.590
What happened to them?

00:20:52.240 --> 00:20:53.530
Flowers, you see,

00:20:53.530 --> 00:20:56.200
want the sun to shine on them.

00:20:56.580 --> 00:20:59.870
They probably didn't like being
wrapped in the apron.

00:21:01.010 --> 00:21:01.830
Really?

00:21:03.790 --> 00:21:05.170
Poor things.

00:21:14.410 --> 00:21:17.550
I'm sorry.
I will never pick flowers again.

00:21:24.690 --> 00:21:25.800
Goodbye.

00:21:30.070 --> 00:21:36.490
<i>Heidi's heart bleeds for the flowers
that has all withered.</i>

00:21:37.120 --> 00:21:41.040
<i>But by dinner time, she has
regained her cheerfulness.</i>

00:21:41.130 --> 00:21:46.210
<i>She tells her grandfather about all
the things that happened on the mountain.</i>

00:21:47.000 --> 00:21:50.670
Say, why do hawks screech like that
and scream towards the ground?

00:21:53.230 --> 00:21:54.400
The hawks, you see,...

00:21:54.400 --> 00:21:57.860
they are laughing at the people in this world
for living so closely jumbled together...

00:21:57.860 --> 00:22:01.650
and getting angry at each other.

00:22:01.830 --> 00:22:03.850
They're laughing?

00:22:03.850 --> 00:22:08.130
That's right. They laugh towards
the ground, saying:

00:22:08.720 --> 00:22:12.760
You people should also stand on
your own, and go your own way.

00:22:12.810 --> 00:22:18.230
Flying high in the sky like me,
you can surely obtain happiness!

00:22:21.360 --> 00:22:22.480
<i>That's right.</i>

00:22:22.570 --> 00:22:29.490
<i>Grandfather lives away from the village people
in this high mountain cabin like a hawk.</i>

00:22:29.740 --> 00:22:35.580
<i>While speaking about hawks,
Grandfather is voicing his own thoughts.</i>

00:22:45.750 --> 00:22:50.290
When we were coming home, it looked
like the mountains were on fire,

00:22:50.290 --> 00:22:54.600
but then they turned rosy-red and after
that the color disappeared.

00:22:54.600 --> 00:22:56.170
What was that?

00:22:56.760 --> 00:22:58.580
Why does that happen?

00:23:00.570 --> 00:23:03.990
That is... because of the sun.

00:23:05.080 --> 00:23:08.160
When he says good-night
to the mountains,

00:23:08.160 --> 00:23:11.870
he throws his most beautiful colors over
them so that they may not forget him

00:23:12.490 --> 00:23:16.010
before he comes again the next day.

00:23:17.870 --> 00:23:19.050
Really?

00:23:19.180 --> 00:23:21.960
That's why it was so pretty.

00:23:21.960 --> 00:23:25.620
Then I will be able to see it again
tomorrow, won't I, Grandfather?

00:23:25.620 --> 00:23:28.780
Yes, you'll see it.
Now, eat up.

00:23:28.850 --> 00:23:29.480
Yes.

00:23:31.780 --> 00:23:36.300
<i>That night, in her comfortable
bed of hay,</i>

00:23:36.300 --> 00:23:42.260
<i>Heidi dreams of sparkling mountains
and red roses on top of them.</i>

00:23:42.470 --> 00:23:48.390
<i>In her dreams, Snowflake is happily
jumping and running around.</i>

00:23:54.490 --> 00:23:57.600
<i>Summer has also arrived at the
mountain cabin on the Alps.</i>

00:23:57.680 --> 00:24:02.600
<i>One summer day, Heidi suddenly encounters
a storm while out on the mountain.</i>

00:24:02.770 --> 00:24:05.390
<i>It's a very frightening mountain storm.</i>

00:24:06.150 --> 00:24:12.030
<i>After the storm is gone, Heidi finds an injured
baby bird underneath a large tree.</i>

00:24:12.190 --> 00:24:18.490
<i>Heidi names the cute chick "Pichi",
and decides to raise it herself.</i>

00:24:18.870 --> 00:24:22.740
<i>From the next day on, Heidi runs around the
mountains and meadows of the alps,</i>

00:24:22.790 --> 00:24:25.910
<i>looking for worms to feed Pichi.</i>

00:24:26.290 --> 00:24:29.290
<i>Next time:
Another Family Member</i>

00:24:29.290 --> 00:24:30.540
<i>Please look forward to it!</i>

